Website rebuild (galton_hoard/webrebuild) and the agent-bench entry "websitebench"

* The scoring rule (a case passes when its functional checks pass and every visual
  checkpoint reaches a flat-baseline-normalized RGB SSIM of 0.99; a site's score is the
  share of its cases that pass) and the idea of rebuilding a site that the agent can
  only explore through a browser follow WebsiteBench, by the WebsiteBench Authors
  (TIGER-AI-Lab), https://github.com/TIGER-AI-Lab/WebsiteBench, released under the
  Apache License 2.0. No code of WebsiteBench is included: the scorer, the step runner,
  the agent loop and the four local reference sites are written here.
* "webrebuild_websitebench action=import" downloads WebsiteBench's public release index,
  its LICENSE and NOTICE and, per task, its instruction, task file and case manifest into
  the data folder, next to a CREDITS.txt. Those files keep their licence (Apache-2.0).
  The reference websites reproduce third-party sites; their content belongs to its
  owners and is provided by WebsiteBench for non-commercial research only.
* The agent-bench entry "websitebench" names the published dataset
  websitebench/WebsiteBench@v1 of the trial runner's registry; the runner downloads and
  runs it in its containers.
